# Example rules configuration for dns-nftsetter
# Format: <source_pattern> / <domain> / <nftables_set_name>

# 1. Client-Specific Pair Rules:
# DNS queries from 192.168.1.100 for *.apple.com (and apple.com) will add the element
# client_ip . resolved_ip to pair_dynamic set (type ipv4_addr . ipv4_addr)
# 192.168.1.100 / apple.com / pair_dynamic

# 2. Any-Client Pair Rules:
# DNS queries from any client for *.google.com will add
# client_ip . resolved_ip to pair_dynamic set
# * / google.com / pair_dynamic

# 3. Global Single IP Rules:
# DNS queries from any client for *.fb.com will add the resolved IP to
# global_dynamic set directly (type ipv4_addr)
# *! / fb.com / global_dynamic
